的"],[137,"resume","rɪˈzjum","v.","恢復；重新開始"],[138,"compatible","kəmˈpætəbl","a.","相容的"],[139,"undergo","ˌʌndɚˈgo","v.","經歷；遭受"],[140,"normally","ˈnɔrməlɪ","ad.","正常地；通常"],[141,"accurately","ˈækjərɪtlɪ","ad.","準確地；精確地"],[142,"regard","rɪˈgɑrd","v.","看待；視為"],[143,"replacement","rɪˈplesmənt","n.","替代品；更換"],[144,"sustain","səˈsten","v.","維持；持續"],[145,"through","θru","prep.","透過；憑藉"],[146,"available","əˈveləbl","a.","可取得的"],[147,"consequential","ˌkɑnsəˈkwɛnʃəl","a.","重大的"],[148,"last","læst","v.","持續；維持"],[149,"forever","fəˈrɛvɚ","ad.","永遠；長久地"],[150,"benefit","ˈbɛnəfɪt","n.","益處；好處"],[151,"transient","ˈtrænʃənt","a.","短暫的"],[152,"interim","ˈɪntərɪm","a.","過渡期的"],[153,"await","əˈwet","v.","等待；期待"],[154,"donor","ˈdonɚ","n.","捐贈者；捐血者"],[155,"roughly","ˈrʌflɪ","ad.","大約；粗略地"],[156,"genetically","dʒəˈnɛtɪkḷɪ","ad.","從基因上"],[157,"modify","ˈmɑdəˌfaɪ","v.","修改；改造"],[158,"eventually","ɪˈvɛntʃʊəlɪ","ad.","最終；最後"],[159,"viable","ˈvaɪəbl","a.","切實可行的"],[160,"option","ˈɑpʃən","n.","選擇；選項"],[161,"alleviate","əˈlivɪˌet","v.","緩解；減輕"],[162,"severe","səˈvɪr","a.","嚴重的；劇烈的"],[163,"shortage","ˈʃɔrtɪdʒ","n.","短缺；不足"],[164,"manufacture","ˌmænjəˈfæktʃɚ","v.","製造；生產"],[165,"decade","ˈdɛked","n.","十年；十年間"],[166,"compatible","kəmˈpætəbl","a.","相容的"],[167,"no longer","no ˈlɔŋgɚ","ph.","不再；已不"],[168,"compete","kəmˈpit","v.","競爭；對抗"]],"S":[{"a":0,"h":"第 1 段","p":[["@When Human Kidneys Are Not Enough: 271 Days of Hope from a Pig Kidney","當人類腎臟不足以應付挑戰：豬腎帶來的 271 天希望"],["Every day, the [kidneys|1] [perform|2] one of the body's most [vital|3] [tasks|4]: [filtering|5] the blood and [eliminating|6] waste and [excess|7] [fluid|8].","腎臟每天都在執行人體最重要的任務之一：過濾血液，清除廢物和多餘水分。"],["Yet this [intricate|9] system can [gradually|10] [deteriorate|11] under three [prevalent|12] health problems — [elevated|13] blood [glucose|14] levels ([hyperglycemia|15]), [hypertension|16], and high [cholesterol|17].","然而，在三種常見的健康問題——高血糖、高血壓和高膽固醇——的影響下，這個精確的系統會逐漸衰退。"],["Over time, [chronic|18] [hyperglycemia|19] damages the [microscopic|20] [blood vessels|21] and [filtering|22] [structures|23] inside the kidneys, while [hypertension|24] can [exacerbate|25] the problem by placing [persistent|26] pressure on the [renal|27] blood vessels.","隨著時間的推移，慢性高血糖會損害腎臟內部的微小血管和過濾結構，而高血壓則會透過持續壓迫腎血管加劇這個問題。"],["High levels of LDL [cholesterol|28] also [contribute to|29] [fatty|30] [deposits|31] inside the [arteries|32], a process known as [atherosclerosis|33], making the vessels [narrower|34] and less [flexible|35].","高水平的低密度脂蛋白膽固醇（LDL-C）也會導致動脈內壁脂"]]},{"a":1,"h":"第 2 段","p":[["Not only can these conditions [impair|36] renal [function|37], but they can also elevate the risk of [heart attack|38] and [stroke|39].","這些疾病不僅會損害腎功能，還會增加心臟病和中風的風險。"],["They [frequently|40] [coexist|41], leaving some patients with kidney disease, [vascular|42] damage, and [cardiovascular|43] [complications|44] [simultaneously|45].","它們常常同時存在，導致一些患者同時患有腎臟疾病、血管損傷和心血管併發症。"],["Once the kidneys can no longer function [adequately|46], patients may [require|47] [dialysis|48] for hours several times a week.","一旦腎臟衰竭，患者可能需要每週數次、每次數小時進行透析。"],["A kidney [transplant|49] can [substantially|50] [enhance|51] their [quality of life|52], but there is one [fundamental|53] [obstacle|54]: there are simply not enough human kidneys.","腎臟移植可以顯著改善患者的生活質量，但存在一個根本性的障礙：人類腎臟數量嚴重不足。"],["In the United States, more than 50,000 people [were newly added to|55] the kidney transplant [waiting list|56] in 2024, while only 27,660 kidney transplants were performed.","在美國，2024 年新增腎臟移植等待名單人數超過 5 萬人，而實際進行的腎臟移植手術僅有 27,660 例。"]]},{"a":2,"h":"第 3 段","p":[["By 2026, [roughly|57] 95,000 Americans were still waiting for a kidney, revealing a [striking|58] [disparity|59] between supply and demand. [Advanced|60] though [transplant|61] medicine has become, it cannot [overcome|62] the [persistent|63] [scarcity|64] of organs.","到 2026 年，仍有約 9.5 萬美國人等待腎臟移植，凸顯了供需之間巨大的巨大差距。儘管移植醫學取得了長足進步，但仍無法克服器官持續短缺的問題。"],["This shortage has [prompted|65] scientists to [contemplate|66] a question that once sounded like science fiction: Could kidneys from pigs help [address the problem|67]?","這種短缺促使科學家思考一個曾經聽起來像是科幻小說的問題：豬腎能否幫助解決這個問題？"],["In 2024, doctors at Massachusetts General Hospital took an [unprecedented|68] step. Richard “Rick” Slayman, 62, became the first living person to receive a kidney from a [genetically|69] [modified|70] pig.","2024 年，麻省總醫院的醫生們採取了一項前所未有的措施。62 歲的理查「瑞克」史萊曼成為第一位接受基因改造豬腎移植的活人。"]]},{"a":3,"h":"第 4 段","p":[["Slayman had Type 2 [diabetes|71], [hypertension|72], and severe [cardiovascular|73] disease.","斯萊曼患有第二型糖尿病、高血壓和嚴重的心血管疾病。"],["A previous human kidney transplant had [failed|74], [compelling|75] him to return to [dialysis|76], while years of disease had left his blood vessels [fragile|77].","他之前接受過一次腎臟移植手術，但手術失敗，必須重新接受透析治療。多年的疾病也使他的血管變得非常脆弱。"],["His [compromised|78] [physical|79] [condition|80] [therefore|81] made the surgery [particularly|82] [formidable|83].","因此，他當時的身體狀況使手術變得格外艱難。"],["[Against the odds|84], the transplant [succeeded|85]. The pig kidney began producing [urine|86] and filtering his blood, and Slayman recovered [sufficiently|87] to return home.","儘管希望渺茫，但移植手術成功了。豬腎開始產生尿液並過濾血液，斯萊曼康復後得以回家。"],["The case provided [tangible|88] [evidence|89] that an organ from another species could function [effectively|90] inside a living human.","這個案例提供了確鑿的證據，證明來自其他物種的器官可以在活人體內有效發揮作用。"]]},{"a":4,"h":"第 5 段","p":[["About two months later, however, Slayman died. Although his death might have appeared to [indicate|91] failure, there was no [evidence|92] to [substantiate|93] the claim that the pig kidney had caused it. Later information [attributed|94] his death to [cardiac|95] problems.","然而，大約兩個月後，斯萊曼去世了。雖然他的死因看似顯示移植失敗，但並沒有證據證實豬腎是導致他死亡的原因。後來的資料顯示，他的死因是心臟問題。"],["His case [demonstrated|96] that the death of a transplant patient does not [necessarily|97] [signify|98] that the transplanted organ itself has failed.","他的案例表明，移植患者的死亡並不一定意味著移植器官本身已經衰竭。"],["The next major [milestone|99] came with Tim Andrews, whose [end-stage|100] renal disease was [likewise|101] [associated|102] with Type 2 diabetes.","下一個重要的里程碑是提姆安德魯斯的案例，他的末期腎臟病同樣與第二型糖尿病有關。"]]},{"a":5,"h":"第 6 段","p":[["By the [terminal|103] stage of his disease, dialysis had become [indispensable|104] to his survival, and he was told that he might have to [endure|105] a wait of several years for a human kidney.","在他病情晚期，透析已成為他維持生命不可或缺的一部分，醫生告訴他，他可能需要等待數年才能等到人類腎臟。"],["In January 2025, the 66-year-old Andrews [received|106] a [genetically|107] modified pig kidney. Scientists used a Yucatan [miniature|108] pig whose [genome|109] had undergone 69 genetic [modifications|110].","2025 年 1 月，66 歲的安德魯斯接受了基因改造豬腎移植。科學家使用了尤卡坦迷你豬的腎臟，這豬的基因組經過了 69 項基因改造。"],["They [eliminated|111] pig genes likely to [provoke|112] a human [immune|113] [response|114], [incorporated|115] [certain|116] human genes, and [deactivated|117] potentially dangerous [viruses|118].","他們剔除了可能引發人類免疫反應的豬基因，整合了某些人類基因，並使潛在的危險病毒失去活性。"],["The [objective|119] was to [prevent|120] Andrews's immune system from [immediately|121] [perceiving|122] the organ as foreign and launching an attack against it.","目的是為了防止安德魯斯的免疫系統立即將這個器官視為外來物並對其發動攻擊。"]]},{"a":6,"h":"第 7 段","p":[["The kidney soon began to function, [enabling|123] Andrews to live without [regular|124] dialysis. One month became three, then six, while the pig kidney [continued|125] filtering his blood.","腎臟很快就開始發揮作用，使安德魯斯無需定期透析即可生存。一個月後，三個月過去了，六個月過去了，豬腎繼續過濾他的血液。"],["The process was not without [complications|126]. Doctors initially [suppressed|127] signs of immune [rejection|128] by [adjusting|129] his [medication|130].","這個過程並非一帆風順。醫生最初透過調整藥物劑量來抑制免疫排斥反應的跡象。"],["About six months later, however, blood vessels inside the kidney developed damage and [inflammation|131], and its function [progressively|132] [deteriorated|133]. The precise [cause|134] [remained|135] [elusive|136].","然而，大約六個月後，腎臟內的血管出現損傷和炎症，腎功能逐漸惡化。確切病因始終不明。"]]},{"a":7,"h":"第 8 段","p":[["Eventually, after 271 days, the pig kidney was removed, and Andrews [resumed|137] dialysis.","最終，在移植豬腎 271 天后，醫生切除了豬腎，安德魯斯重新開始接受透析治療。"],["But his story did not end there.","但他的故事並未就此結束。"],["Eighty-two days later, a [compatible|138] human donor kidney finally became available. Andrews [underwent|139] the transplant successfully, and as of September 2026, the kidney continued to function [normally|140].","82 天后，終於找到了合適的人類腎源。安德魯斯成功接受了腎臟移植手術，截至 2026 年 9 月，移植的腎臟功能正常。"],["The pig kidney, then, may be more [accurately|141] [regarded|142] not as a failed [replacement|143] but as a bridge. It gave Andrews 271 days without dialysis and [sustained|144] him [through|145] part of the waiting period until a human kidney became [available|146].","因此，與其說豬腎是失敗的替代品，不如說它是一座橋樑。它讓安德魯斯免於透析 271 天，並幫助他度過了等待人類腎源的這段時期。"],["This may be the most [consequential|147] lesson of his case: a pig kidney may not have to [last|148] [forever|149] to save lives.","這或許是他案例中最重要的啟示：豬腎無需永久有效也能挽救生命。"]]},{"a":8,"h":"第 9 段","p":[["Even if its [benefit|150] is [transient|151], an organ that functions safely for several months or a year could serve as an [interim|152] bridge for patients [awaiting|153] human [donors|154].","即使其益處是短暫的，一個能安全運作數月或一年的器官也能為等待人類腎源的患者提供過渡方案。"],["Today, [roughly|155] 95,000 Americans are still waiting for a kidney. If [genetically|156] [modified|157] pig kidneys [eventually|158] become a [viable|159] [option|160], they could help [alleviate|161] the [severe|162] organ [shortage|163] and provide patients with something medicine cannot [manufacture|164] — more time.","如今，大約有 95,000 名美國人仍在等待腎源。如果基因改造的豬腎最終成為可行的選擇，它們將有助於緩解嚴重的器官短缺，並為患者提供醫學無法製造的東西——更多的時間。"],["For [decades|165], patients have waited for a [compatible|166] human kidney to become available.","幾十年來，患者一直在等待合適的人類腎源。"],["One day, they may [no longer|167] have to [compete|168] for one.","或許有一天，他們不再需要為此競爭。"]]}],"K":[[[[0.23,0],[0.63,0.047],[1.07,0.128],[1.68,0.209],[1.79,0.256],[2.14,0.303],[3.25,0.384],[4.75,0.638],[5.1,0.685],[5.38,0.732],[5.5,0.779],[6.2,0.825],[6.52,0.872],[6.92,0.919],[7.33,1]],[[8.38,0],[8.83,0.081],[9.46,0.114],[9.75,0.146],[10.25,0.2